course: dictionary
lesson: 6404
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Muscle can be a part of your body, or it can mean strength. «It takes muscle to lift that» is about strength, because lifting needs power, not a body part.
explain: As a body part, a muscle is stretchy tissue that tightens and relaxes to move your bones. «Muscles grow over months with exercise, food and rest» is about this meaning, because grow, exercise and rest all describe your body. A good check is to swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Muscular is the adjective, and it means having strong muscles. Muscle in is informal and means pushing your way into something that is not yours. Always ask: which meaning fits the clues around the word?
fact: A muscle is stretchy tissue that tightens and relaxes to move bones and body parts.
fact: You have over 600 muscles in your body.
fact: The heart is a muscle that never stops working.
fact: «Muscle» can also mean strength, as in «It takes muscle to lift that».
fact: Warm up before sport to help avoid pulling a muscle.
exercise: «It takes muscle to lift that.» In this sentence, what does muscle mean? | A bone in the arm | A type of cereal | *Strength | A game played in school
exercise: «The heart is a muscle that never stops.» Which of these is a muscle that never stops? | Your fingernails | Your hair | Your front teeth | *The heart
exercise: Which word means having strong muscles? | Mustard | *Muscular | Musical | Muddy
test: Biceps and triceps are two muscles that work in what? | Silence | Rows | Circles | *Pairs
test: Which is a good way to avoid pulling a muscle? | Run without warming up | *Warm up before sport | Eat sweets all day | Sit still for hours before a game
exam: «Muscles grow over months with exercise, food and rest», so what helps muscles grow? | *Exercise, food and rest over months | Shouting loudly | Sleeping for one hour | Eating spinach for one day only
